advise|recommend|VERB|suggest a suitable action|To tell someone what you think they should do or what action would be suitable.|khuyên; tư vấn|The guide advised us to carry extra water for the walk.|Hướng dẫn viên khuyên chúng tôi mang thêm nước cho chuyến đi bộ.|Advise someone to do something; advise doing something is used without a named person.|0
gold|metal|NOUN|valuable yellow metal|A valuable yellow metal used in jewellery and other objects.|vàng; kim loại vàng|The jeweller weighed the gold before shaping the ring.|Thợ kim hoàn cân vàng trước khi tạo hình chiếc nhẫn.|Usually uncountable for the material; made of gold names the substance.|0
gold|colour|ADJECTIVE|having a golden colour|Having the colour of gold.|màu vàng óng|Gold curtains made the small stage look brighter.|Những tấm rèm màu vàng óng khiến sân khấu nhỏ trông sáng hơn.|Before a noun or after a linking verb for colour; gold-coloured does not necessarily mean made of the metal.|1
mandate|authority|NOUN|authority to carry out a task|Authority given to a person or organization to carry out a particular task or policy.|thẩm quyền được giao; nhiệm vụ được ủy quyền|The committee has a mandate to review the building plans.|Ủy ban được giao nhiệm vụ xem xét các bản thiết kế công trình.|Countable; a mandate to do something specifies the authorized task, while a mandate from names who gives authority.|0
rumor|unverified-story|NOUN|unconfirmed story passed around|A story or claim that people pass on without knowing whether it is true.|tin đồn|A rumor about the shop's closure spread before the owner spoke.|Tin đồn về việc cửa hàng đóng cửa lan truyền trước khi chủ cửa hàng lên tiếng.|Countable or uncountable; American spelling rumor, British rumour. A rumor is unconfirmed, not necessarily false.|-
united|acting-together|ADJECTIVE|joined by a common aim|Joined together or in agreement about a shared purpose.|đoàn kết; thống nhất|The neighbours remained united in their effort to protect the garden.|Những người hàng xóm vẫn đoàn kết trong nỗ lực bảo vệ khu vườn.|United in an effort or united against a threat names the shared action or opposition.|0
